{:edb/db-before-t 1657 :edb/db-after-t 1658 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534970 50 #inst "2026-10-08T12:34:34.849Z" 13194139534970 true] [17592186129185 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323614 13194139534970 true] [17592186129186 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323607 13194139534970 true] [17592186129186 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323622 13194139534970 true] [17592186129187 1020 #edb/ref 17592186323625 13194139534970 true] [17592186286071 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323621 13194139534970 true] [17592186323607 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323608 13194139534970 true] [17592186323607 1089 "q-136355" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323607 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534970 true] [17592186323607 1100 "The initial velocity of a particle is $(5i+3j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the speed of the particle after $3$ seconds if the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(-i+2j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ Round your answer to two decimal places." 13194139534970 true] [17592186323607 1113 #uuid "b1f34d54-8942-568b-886d-8135a1e4e0a3" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323607 1145 "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=5i+3j,\\,a=-i+2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $3$ seconds, the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(5i+3j)+(-i+2j)(3) \\\\  & =(5i+3j)+(-3i+6j) \\\\  & =(2i+9j)\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v| & =|2i+9j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{9}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+81} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{85} \\\\  & ≈9.22\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places." 13194139534970 true] [17592186323608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323609 13194139534970 true] [17592186323608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323610 13194139534970 true] [17592186323608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323611 13194139534970 true] [17592186323608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323612 13194139534970 true] [17592186323608 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323613 13194139534970 true] [17592186323608 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534970 true] [17592186323608 1041 "selection" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323608 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323613 13194139534970 true] [17592186323608 1110 #uuid "10b55310-aae7-53f6-91e1-ebff7d9c5627" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323609 1034 "8.34\\,\\text{m/s}" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323609 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534970 true] [17592186323609 1111 #uuid "f164bdea-b9b5-5b1e-9ce8-6474703ea3a6" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323610 1034 "8.77\\,\\text{m/s}" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323610 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534970 true] [17592186323610 1111 #uuid "43c67b22-400b-586e-8f0e-b8a925f02649" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323611 1034 "9.45\\,\\text{m/s}" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323611 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534970 true] [17592186323611 1111 #uuid "8fd9f350-9563-54f5-acc5-d4d715be543c" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323612 1034 "10.12\\,\\text{m/s}" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323612 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534970 true] [17592186323612 1111 #uuid "1c941c65-766c-5661-a208-70f90b77673e" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323613 1034 "9.22\\,\\text{m/s}" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323613 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534970 true] [17592186323613 1111 #uuid "513e402a-22be-57c8-be5b-487b288dbabf" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323614 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323615 13194139534970 true] [17592186323614 1089 "q-136376" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323614 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534970 true] [17592186323614 1100 "A particle moves with constant acceleration. When $t=0\\,\\text{s},$ the velocity of the particle is $(5i+j)\\,\\text{ft/s},$ and when $t=4\\,\\text{s},$ the velocity of the particle is $(5i+13j)\\,\\text{ft/s}.$ Calculate the acceleration of the particle." 13194139534970 true] [17592186323614 1113 #uuid "c0106504-81c0-5de5-bc00-12192706f1e0" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323614 1145 "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nu=5i+j,\\,v=5i+13j,\\,t=4,\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $a,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 5i+13j & =(5i+j)+a(4) \\\\ 12j & =4a \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{4}(12j) \\\\  & =3j\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323616 13194139534970 true] [17592186323615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323617 13194139534970 true] [17592186323615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323618 13194139534970 true] [17592186323615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323619 13194139534970 true] [17592186323615 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323620 13194139534970 true] [17592186323615 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534970 true] [17592186323615 1041 "selection" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323615 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323618 13194139534970 true] [17592186323615 1110 #uuid "836eced1-931a-5656-98ea-f88c3efa441e" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323616 1034 "-j\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323616 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534970 true] [17592186323616 1111 #uuid "524af600-4737-53fa-9092-c1c248e8c649" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323617 1034 "-2j\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323617 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534970 true] [17592186323617 1111 #uuid "c31ef56c-a7bb-5530-b6dc-a772beccf517" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323618 1034 "3j\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323618 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534970 true] [17592186323618 1111 #uuid "7c0bb2bf-868a-5e7a-a69f-d26c9fcdf8cb" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323619 1034 "0\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323619 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534970 true] [17592186323619 1111 #uuid "13e08e36-19d7-5137-ab73-3fa15d325384" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323620 1034 "2i\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323620 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534970 true] [17592186323620 1111 #uuid "e702caaf-c263-5fda-a390-c0026e3b9541" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323621 1034 "1" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323621 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534970 true] [17592186323621 1111 #uuid "6b5e3656-999e-5b37-87e5-1b72a59f5252" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323622 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323623 13194139534970 true] [17592186323622 1089 "q-319037" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323622 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534970 true] [17592186323622 1100 "The initial velocity of a particle is $(2i+5j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the **exact** speed of the particle after $3$ seconds if the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(-3i+j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\n$|v|=$\n\n{{field-1}} $\\text{m/s}.$" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323622 1113 #uuid "337fe7e5-2886-56fa-9ae7-af043910f934" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323622 1145 "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=2i+5j,\\,a=-3i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t=3\\,\\text{s},$ the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(2i+5j)+(-3i+j)(3) \\\\  & =(2i+5j)+(-9i+3j) \\\\  & =(-7\\,i+8\\,j)\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v| & =|-7i+8j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-7)^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{113}\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323623 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323624 13194139534970 true] [17592186323623 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534970 true] [17592186323623 1041 "field-1" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323623 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323624 13194139534970 true] [17592186323623 1110 #uuid "62779e9b-d4b6-50b2-b1ed-9b5b51f36755" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323624 1034 "\\sqrt{113}" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323624 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534970 true] [17592186323624 1111 #uuid "de3916e5-f979-5e97-8825-d1e23bd23e1c" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323625 1017 #edb/ref 17592186323626 13194139534970 true] [17592186323625 1089 "q-319169" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323625 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534970 true] [17592186323625 1100 "A particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(-2i+4j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}.$ The velocity of the particle is $(10i-8j)\\,\\text{km/h}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{h}.$ Find the time when the velocity of the particle equals $(-8i+28j)\\,\\text{km/h}.$\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,\\text{h}$" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323625 1113 #uuid "0e91f25b-d36d-54f0-9adb-0e2a79068ce0" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323625 1145 "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nu=10i-8j,\\,v=-8i+28j,\\,a=-2i+4j,\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ -8i+28j & =10i-8j+(-2i+4j)t \\\\ -18i+36j & =(-2i+4j)t \\\\ -18i+36j & =-2ti+4tj\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the $i$ and $j$ components in the last equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-18=-2t \\\\ 36=4t\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,t=9\\,\\text{h}.\n$$" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323626 1000 #edb/ref 17592186323627 13194139534970 true] [17592186323626 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534970 true] [17592186323626 1041 "field-1" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323626 1104 #edb/ref 17592186323627 13194139534970 true] [17592186323626 1110 #uuid "69985783-15dd-5a28-8e98-8f9cbe901597" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323627 1034 "9" 13194139534970 true] [17592186323627 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 1319413953497